  @keyframes foundry-marquee-scroll {
    from { transform: translateX(0); }
    to   { transform: translateX(-50%); }
  }
  #foundry-marquee .marquee-track {
    animation: foundry-marquee-scroll var(--marquee-duration, 90s) linear infinite;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  #foundry-marquee:hover .marquee-track {
    animation-play-state: paused;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #foundry-marquee .marquee-track { animation: none; }
  }
</style>

</section>
<section class="px-[1lh] pb-24">
  <div class="pt-3.5 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.06em] tabular-nums text-black/55 border-t border-black/20">
  How to sell your fonts on Fontdue
</div>
  <div class="m-0 mt-10 leading-[1.55] text-black/55 max-w-[640px] [&_a]:!text-black [&_a]:underline [&_a:hover]:opacity-60 [&_p]:m-0">
    
<p>Your free trial covers everything you need to get selling – here’s how it goes.</p>

  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-start">
    <div class="md:col-span-5">
      <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr gap-3 mb-8">
        <button type="button" data-stories-step="0" data-stories-end="205" data-active="true" class="group w-full text-left cursor-pointer py-5 -my-3 min-[1720px]:py-0 min-[1720px]:my-0 transition-opacity data-[active=false]:min-[1720px]:opacity-40 min-[1720px]:hover:opacity-100!" aria-label="Step 1: Upload your fonts">
          <div class="h-[3px] bg-black/15 overflow-hidden min-[1720px]:mb-3">
            <div data-stories-bar="0" class="h-full bg-black" style="width: 0%"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 1
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block text-[16px] leading-[1.2]">Upload your fonts</div>
        </button><button type="button" data-stories-step="1" data-stories-end="359" data-stories-start="212" data-active="false" class="group w-full text-left cursor-pointer py-5 -my-3 min-[1720px]:py-0 min-[1720px]:my-0 transition-opacity data-[active=false]:min-[1720px]:opacity-40 min-[1720px]:hover:opacity-100!" aria-label="Step 2: Set up your licenses">
          <div class="h-[3px] bg-black/15 overflow-hidden min-[1720px]:mb-3">
            <div data-stories-bar="1" class="h-full bg-black" style="width: 0%"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 2
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block text-[16px] leading-[1.2]">Set up your licenses</div>
        </button><button type="button" data-stories-step="2" data-stories-end="715" data-active="false" class="group w-full text-left cursor-pointer py-5 -my-3 min-[1720px]:py-0 min-[1720px]:my-0 transition-opacity data-[active=false]:min-[1720px]:opacity-40 min-[1720px]:hover:opacity-100!" aria-label="Step 3: Sell your fonts">
          <div class="h-[3px] bg-black/15 overflow-hidden min-[1720px]:mb-3">
            <div data-stories-bar="2" class="h-full bg-black" style="width: 0%"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 3
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block text-[16px] leading-[1.2]">Sell your fonts</div>
        </button><button type="button" data-stories-step="3" data-stories-end="1019" data-stories-start="720" data-active="false" class="group w-full text-left cursor-pointer py-5 -my-3 min-[1720px]:py-0 min-[1720px]:my-0 transition-opacity data-[active=false]:min-[1720px]:opacity-40 min-[1720px]:hover:opacity-100!" aria-label="Step 4: Get paid">
          <div class="h-[3px] bg-black/15 overflow-hidden min-[1720px]:mb-3">
            <div data-stories-bar="3" class="h-full bg-black" style="width: 0%"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 4
          </div>
          <div class="hidden min-[1720px]:block text-[16px] leading-[1.2]">Get paid</div>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="relative min-h-[140px] min-[1720px]:min-h-[72px]">
        <div data-stories-desc="0" class="">
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 1
          </div>
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden text-[18px] leading-[1.2] mb-2.5">Upload your fonts</div>
          <div class="text-black/70 leading-[1.55] max-w-[420px] [&_p]:m-0">
            
<p>Drop in your font files. Fontdue organizes them into collections and generates webfonts automatically. Build type testers and specimen content for each family with our purpose-built CMS.</p>

          </div>
        </div><div data-stories-desc="1" class="hidden">
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 2
          </div>
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden text-[18px] leading-[1.2] mb-2.5">Set up your licenses</div>
          <div class="text-black/70 leading-[1.55] max-w-[420px] [&_p]:m-0">
            
<p>Choose from our presets for desktop, web and app licenses, or build your own configurations with custom variables and options.</p>

          </div>
        </div><div data-stories-desc="2" class="hidden">
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 3
          </div>
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden text-[18px] leading-[1.2] mb-2.5">Sell your fonts</div>
          <div class="text-black/70 leading-[1.55] max-w-[420px] [&_p]:m-0">
            
<p>Customers buy directly from your site with our drop-in store components. Every order lands in your Fontdue admin, tracked and fulfilled automatically.</p>

          </div>
        </div><div data-stories-desc="3" class="hidden">
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden font-mono text-xs text-black/55 uppercase tracking-[0.04em] tabular-nums mb-1.5">
            Step 4
          </div>
          <div class="min-[1720px]:hidden text-[18px] leading-[1.2] mb-2.5">Get paid</div>
          <div class="text-black/70 leading-[1.55] max-w-[420px] [&_p]:m-0">
            
<p>Payments go straight to your own Stripe account. Watch your revenue grow in the dashboard while payouts arrive automatically.</p>

          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-5">
        
<a href="/docs/overview/first-steps" class="!text-black inline-block px-3.5 py-[7px] bg-lime hover:opacity-85 transition-opacity !no-underline">
  Read the full tutorial
</a>

      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-7">
      <button type="button" data-stories-advance class="group relative block w-full text-left cursor-pointer border border-black/15" aria-label="Continue">
        <video id="how-it-works-video" muted playsinline preload="auto" poster="/images/how-it-works-poster.webp" data-stories-fps="30" class="block w-full h-auto">
          <source src="/videos/how-it-works.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
        <span data-stories-overlay hidden class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/60 transition-opacity">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-2.5 text-[16px] leading-[1.4] text-lime group-hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity">
            <span data-stories-overlay-label>Next →</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>
  (function() {
    var video = document.getElementById('how-it-works-video');
    if (!video) return;
    var bars = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-stories-bar]'));
    var steps = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-stories-step]'));
    var descs = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-stories-desc]'));
    var advanceBtn = document.querySelector('[data-stories-advance]');
    var overlay = document.querySelector('[data-stories-overlay]');
    var overlayLabel = document.querySelector('[data-stories-overlay-label]');
    if (!bars.length || !descs.length) return;

    // Chapter end times. Each step carries its last frame in
    // data-stories-end; convert with fps. Steps without one fall back to
    // an even split. The final chapter always ends at the true video end,
    // so an end frame past the last frame simply clamps.
    var count = bars.length;
    var fps = parseFloat(video.dataset.storiesFps) || 30;
    function computeBoundaries(d) {
      var b = [];
      for (var k = 0; k < count; k++) {
        var el = steps[k];
        var ef = el ? parseFloat(el.dataset.storiesEnd) : NaN;
        if (!isNaN(ef) && fps > 0) b.push(Math.min(ef / fps, d));
        else b.push(((k + 1) / count) * d);
      }
      if (count > 0) b[count - 1] = d;
      return b;
    }
    var boundaries = computeBoundaries(15);
    function recalcBoundaries() {
      var d = video.duration;
      if (!isFinite(d) || d <= 0) return;
      boundaries = computeBoundaries(d);
    }
    video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', recalcBoundaries);
    if (!isNaN(video.duration) && video.duration > 0) recalcBoundaries();

    var currentChapter = 0;
    // Autoplay walks through every chapter and loops. Picking a step tab
    // hands control to the visitor: from then on the video parks at each
    // chapter end and the overlay's Next button advances it.
    var autoplay = true;
    // True while a chapter seek is in flight, so the boundary check in
    // tick() doesn't fire on the stale currentTime (e.g. wrapping from
    // the final chapter back to the first).
    var seeking = false;

    function chapterStart(i) {
      var el = steps[i];
      var sf = el ? parseFloat(el.dataset.storiesStart) : NaN;
      if (!isNaN(sf) && fps > 0) {
        var d = video.duration;
        var t = sf / fps;
        return (isFinite(d) && d > 0) ? Math.min(t, d) : t;
      }
      return i === 0 ? 0 : boundaries[i - 1];
    }

    function showChapter(i) {
      descs.forEach(function(el, idx) {
        el.classList.toggle('hidden', idx !== i);
      });
      steps.forEach(function(el, idx) {
        el.dataset.active = idx === i ? 'true' : 'false';
      });
    }

    // Overlay label depends on state: parked mid-chapter (e.g. autoplay was
    // blocked) invites a tap to play the current chapter; parked at a
    // boundary offers the next chapter, or a replay on the final one.
    function overlayText() {
      var atEnd = video.currentTime >= boundaries[currentChapter] - 0.05;
      if (!atEnd) return 'Play ▶';
      return currentChapter === boundaries.length - 1 ? 'Replay ↻' : 'Next →';
    }

    function setOverlay(visible) {
      if (!overlay) return;
      if (visible && overlayLabel) overlayLabel.textContent = overlayText();
      overlay.hidden = !visible;
    }

    function tick() {
      var t = video.currentTime;
      var end = boundaries[currentChapter];

      // At the end of the active chapter: roll on to the next one while
      // autoplaying, otherwise park and wait for a click to advance.
      if (t >= end && !seeking) {
        if (autoplay) {
          goTo(currentChapter + 1);
        } else if (!video.paused) {
          video.pause();
          try { video.currentTime = end; } catch (e) {}
        }
      }

      bars.forEach(function(bar, i) {
        var prev = chapterStart(i);
        var span = boundaries[i] - prev;
        var p;
        if (i < currentChapter) p = 1;
        else if (i > currentChapter) p = 0;
        else p = span > 0 ? Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - prev) / span)) : 0;
        bar.style.width = (p * 100) + '%';
      });

      requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(tick);

    function kickPlay() {
      var p = video.play();
      if (p && p.then) {
        p.then(function() { setOverlay(false); })
         .catch(function() { setOverlay(true); });
      }
    }

    // iOS Safari freezes the decoder when play() is called while a seek is
    // still in flight: the clock advances (so the progress bar grows) but no
    // new frames paint. The video is muted, so autoplay policy lets us start
    // playback from the 'seeked' callback - seek first, then play.
    function seekAndPlay(t) {
      if (Math.abs(video.currentTime - t) < 0.04) {
        kickPlay();
        return;
      }
      seeking = true;
      var done = false;
      function go() {
        if (done) return;
        done = true;
        seeking = false;
        video.removeEventListener('seeked', go);
        kickPlay();
      }
      video.addEventListener('seeked', go);
      // Safety net in case 'seeked' never arrives.
      setTimeout(go, 800);
      try { video.currentTime = t; } catch (e) { go(); }
    }

    function goTo(i) {
      currentChapter = ((i % boundaries.length) + boundaries.length) % boundaries.length;
      showChapter(currentChapter);
      seekAndPlay(chapterStart(currentChapter));
    }

    function advance() {
      // Clicking the video while it plays stops it and takes over from
      // autoplay; the overlay then offers Play / Next / Replay.
      if (!video.paused) {
        autoplay = false;
        video.pause();
        return;
      }
      // Parked mid-chapter (autoplay was blocked, say) - resume the current
      // chapter rather than skipping ahead. Only advance from a boundary.
      var atEnd = video.currentTime >= boundaries[currentChapter] - 0.05;
      if (!atEnd) {
        kickPlay();
        return;
      }
      goTo(currentChapter + 1);
    }

    if (advanceBtn) advanceBtn.addEventListener('click', advance);

    steps.forEach(function(el) {
      el.addEventListener('click', function() {
        var i = parseInt(el.dataset.storiesStep, 10);
        if (isNaN(i)) return;
        autoplay = false;
        goTo(i);
      });
    });

    // While autoplaying, a pause is either a chapter hand-off (goTo seeks
    // and resumes) or blocked autoplay; kickPlay() shows the overlay for
    // the latter, so a plain pause event only matters once a visitor has
    // taken over.
    video.addEventListener('pause', function() { if (!autoplay) setOverlay(true); });
    video.addEventListener('play', function() { setOverlay(false); });

    showChapter(0);

    // Start playback the first time the video scrolls into view.
    var started = false;
    function start() {
      if (started) return;
      started = true;
      kickPlay();
    }
    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
        entries.forEach(function(entry) {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            start();
            io.disconnect();
          }
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.3 });
      io.observe(video);
    } else {
      start();
    }
  })();
</script>

</section>
<section class="px-[1lh] pb-20 scroll-mt-4">
  <div class="pt-3.5 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.06em] tabular-nums text-black/55 border-t border-black/20">
  Features
</div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-start">
    <div class="md:col-span-5 text-sm [&_p]:m-0 [&_p:not(:first-child)]:mt-2.5 [&_p]:leading-[1.55] [&_p]:max-w-[420px] [&_a]:!text-black [&_a]:underline [&_a:hover]:opacity-60 [&>a:not(:first-child)]:mt-5">
      
<p>Fontdue provides a suite of features to help you start and run your foundry, including:</p>
<p><strong>Handling fonts</strong> – process and organize your catalog, generate webfonts, and offer free test fonts.</p>
<p><strong>Selling fonts</strong> – configure licenses, take payments and tax through Stripe, and manage orders, customers, and reports.</p>
<p><strong>Presenting fonts online</strong> – author content, customize your storefront, and drop in components like type testers and the store.</p>
<a href="/docs/overview/what-is-fontdue" class="!text-black inline-block px-3.5 py-[7px] bg-lime hover:opacity-85 transition-opacity !no-underline">
  Explore the platform guide
</a>

    </div>
